From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arbion Halili <a.halili@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 03:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: dax: make the mapping range size configurable

The DAX window is carved into fixed 2 MiB ranges and a file occupies at
least one, so a guest mapping many small files needs a window many
times larger than the data: one system held 566 ranges, 1.1 GiB of
window, for 53 MiB of files. The window is backed by a struct page per
4 KiB at mount, 16 MiB of guest RAM per GiB, whether used or not.

Expose the range size as CONFIG_FUSE_DAX_SHIFT so such guests can pick a
smaller range and fit the same working set into a much smaller window.
The default stays at 21. The range must still be at least the server's
map_alignment, which fuse_dax_check_alignment() already verifies. Ranges
below 2 MiB map with PTEs only; the PMD fault path already falls back
when the iomap extent is shorter than PMD_SIZE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/fs/fuse/Kconfig b/fs/fuse/Kconfig
index 3a4ae63..9a8ae15 100644
--- a/fs/fuse/Kconfig
+++ b/fs/fuse/Kconfig
@@ -54,6 +54,28 @@ config FUSE_DAX
 	  If you want to allow mounting a Virtio Filesystem with the "dax"
 	  option, answer Y.
 
+config FUSE_DAX_SHIFT
+	int "Virtio Filesystem DAX mapping range size (log2 bytes)"
+	depends on FUSE_DAX
+	range 16 30
+	default 21
+	help
+	  The DAX window is handed out to files in fixed-size ranges of
+	  2^FUSE_DAX_SHIFT bytes. A file occupies at least one range however
+	  small it is, so with the 2 MiB default a window has to be many times
+	  larger than the data mapped through it once many small files are
+	  in use. A smaller range lets the same working set fit in a smaller
+	  window; the window itself costs a struct page per 4 KiB of guest
+	  RAM whether or not it is used, so this trades that fixed cost
+	  against more mapping requests for large files.
+
+	  Ranges of at least 2 MiB (21) let the guest map files with huge
+	  pages when the window is suitably aligned; smaller ranges use
+	  PTE-sized mappings only. The server's FUSE_INIT map_alignment must
+	  not exceed this value.
+
+	  If unsure, keep the default of 21.
+
 config FUSE_PASSTHROUGH
 	bool "FUSE passthrough operations support"
 	default y
diff --git a/fs/fuse/dax.c b/fs/fuse/dax.c
index f6cf00a..0e65420 100644
--- a/fs/fuse/dax.c
+++ b/fs/fuse/dax.c
@@ -14,10 +14,11 @@
 #include <linux/interval_tree.h>
 
 /*
- * Default memory range size.  A power of 2 so it agrees with common FUSE_INIT
- * map_alignment values 4KB and 64KB.
+ * Memory range size, as log2 bytes. A power of 2 so it agrees with common
+ * FUSE_INIT map_alignment values 4KB and 64KB; the server's alignment is
+ * checked against it in fuse_dax_check_alignment().
  */
-#define FUSE_DAX_SHIFT	21
+#define FUSE_DAX_SHIFT	CONFIG_FUSE_DAX_SHIFT
 #define FUSE_DAX_SZ	(1 << FUSE_DAX_SHIFT)
 #define FUSE_DAX_PAGES	(FUSE_DAX_SZ / PAGE_SIZE)
 
